1
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:29,946
TAKE CHARGE OF MY HEART

2
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:45,253
No. It's really not what it looks like.

3
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:50,508
Wait.

4
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:53,386
I swear, you've got the wrong idea.

5
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:57,432
I wasn't… trying to kiss you or anything.

6
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:59,809
I was here when I woke up,
and so were you.

7
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,102
Whatever.

8
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:03,730
-Get out.
-No, wait.

9
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:05,732
Listen.

10
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:09,194
Normally, when I do this,

11
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:11,237
you're supposed to feel a tingle.

12
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:14,657
But for some reason,
it doesn't affect you at all--

13
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:18,745
I warned you. This kind of physical
advance makes me uncomfortable.

14
00:01:18,828 --> 00:01:19,954
"Advance"?

15
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:26,586
Look, I know this looks bad, but…

16
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:33,468
I've been trying to explain it to you,
but you just won't hear me out.

17
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:35,386
Get out. Before I call someone.

18
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:36,513
No, I won't!

19
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:40,809
See this? I had my appendix taken out.

20
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:42,227
This is my room.

21
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:45,730
This is a private VIP room.
The one I always stay in.

22
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:49,067
See that? Two beds.

23
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:50,944
I told you, I woke up in this room.

24
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:52,487
I said get out. Now!

25
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:55,490
Ms. Na's hospital room…

26
00:01:57,617 --> 00:01:58,493
is here.

27
00:01:58,576 --> 00:01:59,536
Mr. Jang.

28
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:08,920
You're saying the hospital had a blackout,

29
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:12,173
and my artificial heart
ran out of battery?

30
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:16,970
This smartwatch displays
your heart's remaining battery life.

31
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:22,392
Normally, it should stay fully charged.

32
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:25,854
But now, it's down to 43%.

33
00:02:25,937 --> 00:02:28,356
I can get another surgery
to fix this, right?

34
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:30,358
-Yeah, you could.
-Then…

35
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:31,401
In three months.

36
00:02:33,778 --> 00:02:36,614
Another surgery right now
would be too hard on your body.

37
00:02:36,698 --> 00:02:39,075
The risk of death is too high.

38
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,369
Even if the surgery goes well,

39
00:02:42,203 --> 00:02:45,456
you'll need at least a year to recover.

40
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:46,666
A year?

41
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:51,129
You know I can't wait that long.
I have to…

42
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:53,965
That's exactly why

43
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,177
you need Ms. Na right now.

44
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,262
-Sorry?
-What?

45
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:02,182
Me? All of a sudden?

46
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:03,933
For whatever reason,

47
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:08,897
your heart battery slowly recharges
whenever you're around Ms. Na.

48
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:18,364
Ms. Na Bo-bae said she thinks
the power came back because of her?

49
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:19,407
Yes.

50
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:22,785
I thought she was just rambling
out of fear before the surgery,

51
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:26,247
but the lights really did flicker on
every time her bed passed by.

52
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:27,457
On top of that…

53
00:03:32,212 --> 00:03:35,381
this patient gives off
unusually strong static electricity.

54
00:03:38,092 --> 00:03:38,927
Professor.

55
00:03:39,552 --> 00:03:41,763
I think his heart is charging now.

56
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:44,974
Your heart battery was down to 6%.

57
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:50,355
But how…

58
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:02,283
When you're within
a ten-meter radius of Ms. Na,

59
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:06,204
your heart battery gradually recharges.

60
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,298
Get out.

61
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:19,968
-Wait, my stomach…
-Ho-rang, please.

62
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:22,679
You expect me to believe that nonsense?

63
00:04:24,806 --> 00:04:26,641
Hey, Ho-rang!

64
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:30,520
Jeez, why did he kick me out?

65
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:32,647
Well…

66
00:04:33,147 --> 00:04:36,859
Ho-rang's life is on the line,

67
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:38,695
so he's understandably on edge.

68
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,656
To be honest,
I still find it hard to believe.

69
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:45,743
But right now, you are his lifeline.

70
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:49,247
But he doesn't even want me around, so…

71
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:53,584
What if I'm just a straw, not a lifeline?

72
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:56,504
When you checked his battery charge,

73
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:59,716
didn't you notice anything unusual
about my body?

74
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:03,803
Well, I'd have to run more tests
before I can say for sure,

75
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,597
but it definitely seemed unusual.

76
00:05:07,849 --> 00:05:10,143
But sometimes in life,

77
00:05:10,226 --> 00:05:14,063
even a strange little straw
can save a life.

78
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:25,158
Will you be okay, sir?

79
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:27,535
You'll have to call her back to recharge.

80
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:28,995
You believe that nonsense?

81
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:31,914
How can a human recharge
an artificial heart?

82
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:33,458
Besides,

83
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:36,002
if my surgery's three months away,

84
00:05:37,378 --> 00:05:38,588
what do I tell Grandma?

85
00:05:39,213 --> 00:05:41,591
My aunt and Choi Do-yoon
are already out to get me.

86
00:05:41,674 --> 00:05:45,636
And I still have the anniversary
and Ji Eun-ho to deal with.

87
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,555
Sir, deep breaths.

88
00:05:48,222 --> 00:05:49,766
We can always reschedule.

89
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:51,017
But if we can't adjust--

90
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:54,228
I'll take that into account
and have a Plan Z ready.

91
00:05:55,271 --> 00:05:56,105
Deep breath.

92
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:01,402
Please sit down.

93
00:06:17,710 --> 00:06:19,670
It only dropped by 1%.

94
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:21,547
Are you sure you'll be okay?

95
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:25,843
Yeah.

96
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:28,054
All right.

97
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,056
You should get back to work.

98
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:33,726
Yes, sir. Call me if you need anything.

99
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:35,728
Don't overthink. Just meditate.

100
00:06:36,312 --> 00:06:38,648
Stress and anxiety
are bad for your recovery.

101
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:41,192
Empty your mind completely. Take care.

102
00:07:07,343 --> 00:07:08,719
But sometimes in life,

103
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:13,015
even a strange little straw
can save a life.

104
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:16,602
He has a device inside his body.

105
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:19,939
So that's what absorbed the current?

106
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:50,470
You kicked me out earlier.
Are you looking for me now?

107
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:52,096
Getting a little desperate now?

108
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,266
Can I have a minute?

109
00:08:24,962 --> 00:08:26,797
Hey, hey.

110
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:29,717
You have a chip implanted or something?

111
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,469
Where do you think you're looking?

112
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:33,804
Or

113
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:37,600
did you do… something to me?

114
00:08:37,683 --> 00:08:38,976
Do what?

115
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:42,146
All I did was wake up from surgery
and find myself next to you.

116
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:45,316
Fine. Let's call it
an inexplicable miracle.

117
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:48,444
Stay by my side until my next surgery.

118
00:08:49,028 --> 00:08:51,364
For now, I need you so I can recharge.

119
00:08:51,447 --> 00:08:54,075
What's with that tone?
Are you ordering me around?

120
00:08:56,869 --> 00:08:57,745
Goodness.

121
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:00,831
I'll give you what you want.

122
00:09:00,915 --> 00:09:02,333
What I want?

123
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:18,599
Excuse me.

124
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,519
Could we try just one more time…

125
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:33,072
What are you doing?

126
00:09:33,155 --> 00:09:36,826
You've been wanting to kiss me
all this time!

127
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:38,452
I'll give you what you want.

128
00:09:38,536 --> 00:09:39,495
No, that was…

129
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:41,872
That was…

130
00:09:42,456 --> 00:09:44,208
I just needed to check something.

131
00:09:45,084 --> 00:09:47,044
Now that I know, I don't need to anymore.

132
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:49,505
Now I know it was
because of the artificial heart.

133
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:51,757
That was close.

134
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:58,264
So what do you want right now?

135
00:09:58,347 --> 00:09:59,223
Money?

136
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:00,933
If it's money, that's even easier.

137
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:03,311
How much?

138
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:13,696
If you really want to know what I want,

139
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:18,409
you shouldn't have tried to kiss me
or offered me money.

140
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:20,119
You should've asked me first.

141
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:23,080
Why I kept following you
after that accidental kiss.

142
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:25,124
What I meant by the tingle.

143
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:26,167
Or

144
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:29,086
why I was acting that way.

145
00:10:33,215 --> 00:10:36,427
Well, if being near me recharges you,
I can do that much.

146
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:38,137
Since your life depends on it.

147
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,221
But

148
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,140
that's as far as I go.

149
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:44,644
Being around you is really unpleasant now.

150
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,400
Jeez.

151
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:08,709
What are you doing?
Didn't you hear what I just said?

152
00:11:09,835 --> 00:11:12,755
What's this?

153
00:11:12,838 --> 00:11:13,798
Why, you…

154
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:16,801
I was a tae kwon do black belt as a kid.

155
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:19,053
My retired sister won gold in tae kwon do,

156
00:11:19,136 --> 00:11:20,638
and my brother is a judoka--

157
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:30,981
Let me just check something.

158
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:39,657
Seriously? Unbelievable!

159
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,244
My heart…

160
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:44,870
You damn pervert!

161
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,539
-Why, you…
-No…

162
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:00,553
It actually

163
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:02,680
went up.

164
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:06,350
There have been some studies on it.

165
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:08,853
But it's not conclusive,
so I can't say for sure.

166
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:11,689
What I can tell you now is this.

167
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:15,901
When you're within ten meters
of each other, the battery charges.

168
00:12:16,694 --> 00:12:19,029
The closer you are, the faster it charges.

169
00:12:20,948 --> 00:12:23,409
So you're saying…

170
00:12:25,035 --> 00:12:26,120
Me

171
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:28,205
and that woman

172
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,624
being closer?

173
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,252
You mean physical contact?

174
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:34,420
Exactly.

175
00:12:34,503 --> 00:12:37,923
It'll probably charge fastest

176
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,760
when your mucosal surfaces
come into contact.

177
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:43,804
"Mucosal surfaces"?

178
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:15,336
FULLY CHARGED

179
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:22,051
No way!

180
00:13:22,551 --> 00:13:23,385
Hey.

181
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:24,845
Are you okay?

182
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,180
So you're saying

183
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,225
I have to get physical with that woman…

184
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:33,729
to stay alive.

185
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:37,274
Just like the test shoot.
Look straight ahead.

186
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:38,984
Yes! Great! That's it!

187
00:13:39,068 --> 00:13:41,654
Hold that pose. Eyes on the camera. Good!

188
00:13:42,154 --> 00:13:44,698
Great. Na-min,
move a little closer to Eun-ho.

189
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:46,867
Yes, gaze into each other's eyes.

190
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:48,702
Yes, that's it. Very nice.

191
00:13:48,786 --> 00:13:50,996
Hold that. Look straight ahead. Beautiful.

192
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:54,667
Yes, hold that expression and pose.
That's good.

193
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:58,462
Yes, that looks fantastic.
You're the best!

194
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:00,714
Try crossing your legs.

195
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:03,133
I love it. That's exactly what I wanted.

196
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:05,344
Here we go!

197
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:08,180
Love the look in your eyes.
Tilt your head a little.

198
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:09,974
Nice. That's great. Keep still!

199
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:17,273
Hee-chan, do we have anything after this?

200
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:20,776
You've got shoots until dawn.
Don't even think about going anywhere.

201
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,361
Hello, Mr. Ji Eun-ho.

202
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:30,411
Oh, you can just give it to me.

203
00:14:32,329 --> 00:14:34,373
Hanlim… Hanlim Advertising Company?

204
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:37,585
I'm Ma Hee-chan, Eun-ho's manager.

205
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:39,879
I'm here to make Mr. Ji a great offer.

206
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:42,756
I'd like to speak to you directly.

207
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:44,884
Would that be okay, Mr. Ji?

208
00:14:51,307 --> 00:14:52,892
Oh, my gosh!

209
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:55,185
Jeez. You scared me!

210
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:56,478
Ms. Na Bo-bae.

211
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:59,064
What is it?

212
00:15:01,233 --> 00:15:02,359
I've been thinking.

213
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:03,944
About what now?

214
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:09,074
I think I've been out of line with you
over the past couple of days.

215
00:15:09,658 --> 00:15:10,576
What's wrong?

216
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:13,078
Is your battery drained?
Do you feel like you're dying?

217
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:14,622
This isn't like you.

218
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:16,540
I

219
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:18,208
sincerely

220
00:15:19,418 --> 00:15:20,544
regret what I did.

221
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:23,464
You do?

222
00:15:24,465 --> 00:15:25,591
That's good to hear.

223
00:15:28,761 --> 00:15:29,678
Then

224
00:15:30,429 --> 00:15:33,474
will you forgive me for being rude?

225
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:38,062
I've never been this close to anyone.

226
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:40,731
So you'll

227
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,441
forgive me?

228
00:15:44,652 --> 00:15:45,694
Yeah, well…

229
00:15:46,946 --> 00:15:47,780
Why not?

230
00:15:50,824 --> 00:15:53,494
Then, with mutual courtesy and respect…

231
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,499
let's draw up a contract.

232
00:15:59,083 --> 00:16:00,542
A contract?

233
00:16:01,543 --> 00:16:05,005
To celebrate their 30th anniversary,
TS Resort is looking for a new face.

234
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:08,676
It'll probably lead to becoming
the face of the entire TS Group.

235
00:16:09,259 --> 00:16:11,637
In other words,
you'll be the new face of TS.

236
00:16:13,764 --> 00:16:15,099
It's a provisional contract.

237
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:18,018
One-year contract, with a signing bonus.

238
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:22,272
Wait.

239
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,567
Are you sure this is right?
I think there's an extra zero.

240
00:16:27,152 --> 00:16:28,195
That's correct.

241
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:31,490
That's what TS thinks you're worth.

242
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:34,284
If you want, we can negotiate.

243
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:36,578
A superstar like you
belongs on a bigger stage.

244
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:45,295
A contract stipulating legal and regular
physical contact for three months.

245
00:16:47,881 --> 00:16:50,050
-What contact?
-Physical.

246
00:16:50,134 --> 00:16:53,971
Strictly professional
and non-intimate physical contact.

247
00:16:57,725 --> 00:16:58,642
Well,

248
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:01,812
I have a question.

249
00:17:01,895 --> 00:17:03,856
Sure. Ask me anything.

250
00:17:05,482 --> 00:17:06,483
Are you…

251
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:08,861
out of your mind?

252
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:12,990
I'm perfectly sane.

253
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:15,242
You're not. Your eyes look unhinged.

254
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:16,618
You sound like a lunatic.

255
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:18,579
Are you rejecting my offer?

256
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:20,289
Does this sound like acceptance?

257
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:33,886
A what contract?
Strictly professional? Non-intimate?

258
00:17:36,346 --> 00:17:37,264
I must decline.

259
00:17:38,265 --> 00:17:41,268
I don't do ads,
not for any amount of money.

260
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:45,022
I'd rather focus on acting
than commercial work.

261
00:17:45,105 --> 00:17:48,108
These days,
they want versatile entertainers, Mr. Ji.

262
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:50,611
You know, all-around entertainers.

263
00:17:51,278 --> 00:17:52,488
Well…

264
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:55,491
I'm not trying to be perfect.

265
00:17:56,700 --> 00:18:01,163
Besides, you can usually do just fine
if you excel at one thing.

266
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:11,965
Congratulations.

267
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,634
What for?

268
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:15,803
You're smiling.
I figured you got the contract.

269
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:17,429
Oh.

270
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:19,098
No, not yet.

271
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:21,183
I just find it hilarious.

272
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:23,894
We're just looking for a temporary face,

273
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:26,230
and this kid's already acting
like some big-shot actor.

274
00:18:29,274 --> 00:18:32,569
I really wanted to secure Ji Eun-ho
for Mr. Baek as a get-well gift.

275
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,113
Thank you anyway.

276
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:36,532
Here's your meal.

277
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:37,908
Thank you.

278
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:41,203
Excuse me, ma'am.

279
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:43,872
When can I eat? I'm so hungry.

280
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:45,541
Have you passed gas yet?

281
00:18:45,624 --> 00:18:48,335
I was told to give you food
after you pass gas.

282
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:50,712
No, not yet.

283
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:52,089
Yes, she has.

284
00:18:52,631 --> 00:18:53,465
What?

285
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:55,717
No, I haven't.

286
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,678
Yes, you have. Early yesterday morning.

287
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,596
Pfft.

288
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:16,280
Can you keep it do…

289
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:25,706
So you passed gas.

290
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:29,751
I'll let the nurse know
and bring your meal right away.

291
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:42,181
Good thing I passed gas, right?

292
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:44,933
Did the bed not break?
That was some noise.

293
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:52,858
Where are you going?

294
00:19:53,734 --> 00:19:55,819
None of your fart… I mean, business.

295
00:20:03,869 --> 00:20:05,329
So refreshing.

296
00:20:09,249 --> 00:20:11,418
That was so embarrassing. Damn it.

297
00:20:13,962 --> 00:20:16,506
It's just a bodily function.

298
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:18,842
It just means I'm recovering well.

299
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:24,932
Seriously, I'm so embarrassed.

300
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:26,892
About what?

301
00:20:28,393 --> 00:20:29,478
Eun-ho.

302
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:47,204
Mr. Baek.

303
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:55,087
The chairwoman told me, so I came.

304
00:20:55,170 --> 00:20:57,923
We're business partners now, after all.

305
00:20:59,675 --> 00:21:01,635
But where exactly did you have surgery?

306
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:05,639
My appendix.

307
00:21:06,473 --> 00:21:09,268
I'm not really in any condition
to talk right now.

308
00:21:10,769 --> 00:21:13,021
I just dropped by to see how you're doing.

309
00:21:13,105 --> 00:21:16,233
I heard you were hospitalized,
so I had to come see you.

310
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:18,068
I'll walk you out.

311
00:21:18,151 --> 00:21:20,153
No, it's okay. I just got here.

312
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:22,197
You're not feeling well.

313
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:23,657
I'll stay a bit--

314
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,908
I know you're busy.

315
00:21:24,992 --> 00:21:26,660
I shouldn't keep you.

316
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:38,380
Are you feeling better?

317
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:39,464
Yeah.

318
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:43,552
Is it really okay for you
to come here again like this?

319
00:21:43,635 --> 00:21:45,929
You know you're famous, right?

320
00:21:47,264 --> 00:21:49,850
So what if I am?
Can't I visit a friend in the hospital?

321
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:54,980
You've gotten so thin.

322
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:57,983
Are you sure you're okay?

323
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:01,486
Really?

324
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:02,529
Yeah.

325
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:06,908
No, this isn't from being sick.

326
00:22:07,743 --> 00:22:08,952
It's just…

327
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:12,706
It's from stress. A stress diet.

328
00:22:13,206 --> 00:22:15,542
Why? Is someone giving you a hard time?

329
00:22:17,502 --> 00:22:19,671
Your face looks a bit red too.

330
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:21,465
Is stress making you sick?

331
00:22:22,132 --> 00:22:24,843
Of course it's red.
Your handsome face is so close.

332
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:35,479
Is it because of Director Yeom Min-kyu?

333
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:39,983
Yeah, him too.

334
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,444
Come to think of it, I'm in trouble.

335
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:46,531
He told me to get the romance right
in three months.

336
00:22:46,615 --> 00:22:48,575
He criticized the romance again?

337
00:22:49,242 --> 00:22:51,203
As if he knows anything about it.

338
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:53,205
I like everything you write.

339
00:22:53,288 --> 00:22:55,582
Well, you're a fan.

340
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:58,460
That's why you're so nice about my work.

341
00:22:58,543 --> 00:23:00,754
That damn romance.

342
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:03,590
I'm so sick of it.

343
00:23:04,091 --> 00:23:06,718
Well, if you want… You know…

344
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:11,556
I could help with the romance.

345
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:15,060
You…

346
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:18,438
How are you going to help me
with the romance?

347
00:23:19,439 --> 00:23:22,776
Well, I mean, since I act and stuff…

348
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:23,860
Mr. Baek?

349
00:23:24,986 --> 00:23:25,987
Do you know them?

350
00:23:26,947 --> 00:23:28,907
-No.
-The thing is, the male lead…

351
00:23:29,574 --> 00:23:31,159
I don't know her.

352
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:34,704
But it's not clear who he really is.

353
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,791
He could be the son of a rival boss, or…

354
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:40,127
-Writer Na Bo-bae?
-Yeah.

355
00:23:40,210 --> 00:23:41,920
She's a new writer I'm working with.

356
00:23:42,003 --> 00:23:43,588
Her contract's up in three months.

357
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:46,299
Why are you cleaning that?
It won't be in the shot.

358
00:23:47,717 --> 00:23:49,386
So, about Ms. Na's script…

359
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,304
Is the romance weak?

360
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:55,142
I told her to go fall in love
if that's what it takes to fix the script.

361
00:23:55,225 --> 00:23:57,060
So how do you know her?

362
00:23:57,727 --> 00:23:59,312
Never mind. Bye.

363
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:00,439
Baek Ho-rang!

364
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:02,941
What the heck?

365
00:24:07,154 --> 00:24:11,658
If someone was that desperate
to tell me their story, I'd have asked.

366
00:24:11,741 --> 00:24:12,576
"What's wrong?"

367
00:24:13,285 --> 00:24:15,245
So that's her "story."

368
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:20,917
So she was trying to fix her weak script
by flirting with just about anyone?

369
00:24:26,256 --> 00:24:28,425
Then we should give each other
what we need.

370
00:24:33,472 --> 00:24:35,015
Do you know them?

371
00:24:36,016 --> 00:24:36,892
No.

372
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:40,145
I don't know her.

373
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:45,400
…the male lead becomes a bodyguard.

374
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:47,986
But it's not clear who he really is.

375
00:24:49,404 --> 00:24:51,364
He singled her out and said,

376
00:24:51,990 --> 00:24:53,533
"I don't know her"?

377
00:25:17,724 --> 00:25:20,727
Writer Na Bo-bae?

378
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:28,610
What are you doing here?
You almost scared me to death.

379
00:25:29,277 --> 00:25:30,403
My stomach hurts.

380
00:25:30,904 --> 00:25:33,073
MBS Drama Contest Grand Prize Winner.

381
00:25:33,156 --> 00:25:35,367
Debuted with the TV special Wistful Youth.

382
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:39,496
Spent the last three years developing
a romance miniseries with Director Yeom.

383
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:43,500
Did you do a background check on me?

384
00:25:43,583 --> 00:25:46,336
But the romance isn't convincing,
so you're stuck.

385
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:49,464
I heard your contract's up
in three months.

386
00:25:50,048 --> 00:25:52,008
What's it to you if I'm bad at romance?

387
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:59,140
Was that guy you were talking to outside
your boyfriend?

388
00:26:00,308 --> 00:26:03,019
No, he's just a close friend.

389
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:04,479
Really?

390
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:06,731
In that case,

391
00:26:07,732 --> 00:26:10,986
as you can see, I tick all the boxes.
Objectively speaking.

392
00:26:11,736 --> 00:26:15,031
Looks, wealth, social status, personality.

393
00:26:17,951 --> 00:26:19,119
What's so funny?

394
00:26:19,202 --> 00:26:22,038
Fine, I'll give you everything else.

395
00:26:22,622 --> 00:26:24,291
But your personality?

396
00:26:24,374 --> 00:26:26,751
Actually, wherever I go,

397
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:30,422
people see me as a true gentleman
with great manners.

398
00:26:31,006 --> 00:26:32,757
"A true gentleman."

399
00:26:35,802 --> 00:26:40,098
Anyway, the point is,
I'm used to being hit on.

400
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:43,226
But between work and my heart condition,

401
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:44,936
nothing ever came of it.

402
00:26:46,938 --> 00:26:47,856
Are you bragging?

403
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:50,108
Yeah. To be exact,
I'm trying to impress you.

404
00:26:50,191 --> 00:26:52,068
Romance is my forte.

405
00:26:55,614 --> 00:26:57,032
Let me make you another offer.

406
00:26:57,616 --> 00:27:00,076
Agree to my three-month
physical contact contract

407
00:27:00,744 --> 00:27:03,246
and I may be able to help you

408
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:05,248
with the romance you're so bad at.

409
00:27:07,917 --> 00:27:08,918
What do you say?

410
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:29,773
Ms. Na Bo-bae?

411
00:27:32,192 --> 00:27:33,026
Pardon?

412
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:38,782
What is it? What?

413
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:39,824
Never mind, sir.

414
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:42,869
I brought the documents you wanted.

415
00:27:51,002 --> 00:27:52,379
Ms. Na.

416
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:56,966
You said you'd think it over yesterday.
Have you made up your mind?

417
00:27:58,593 --> 00:28:01,846
I know you're awake.
I can hear you breathing.

418
00:28:06,559 --> 00:28:07,394
Open the curtain.

419
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:09,187
Yes, sir.

420
00:28:13,733 --> 00:28:16,069
She's not here, sir, but…

421
00:28:17,028 --> 00:28:18,405
Emergency Charging Station.

422
00:28:18,488 --> 00:28:21,741
-58-1 Songan-dong, Geumjin-gu, Seoul.
-There's this.

423
00:28:21,825 --> 00:28:23,952
Don't come unless you're about to die.

424
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:26,871
"Emergency Charging Station"?

425
00:28:31,251 --> 00:28:34,587
He's still unwell.
Maybe I shouldn't have left so soon.

426
00:28:37,215 --> 00:28:39,300
Whatever. I left my address.

427
00:28:39,384 --> 00:28:42,303
Honestly, I've done all I can for him.

428
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:45,348
All right.

429
00:28:46,474 --> 00:28:49,519
As I-hyeok buckles

430
00:28:50,019 --> 00:28:55,400
Hye-ju's seat belt…

431
00:29:02,741 --> 00:29:05,326
HYE-JU IS SITTING IN THE BACK SEAT,
SEEMINGLY DRUNK

432
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:07,287
Ma'am, please fasten your seat belt.

433
00:29:10,582 --> 00:29:11,458
[POUTING]

434
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:12,792
No, it's uncomfortable.

435
00:29:17,547 --> 00:29:21,259
I-HYEOK STEPS OUT OF THE CAR
AND OPENS THE BACK DOOR

436
00:29:22,802 --> 00:29:23,803
What are you doing?

437
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:24,929
[SECRETLY PLEASED]

438
00:29:26,848 --> 00:29:27,682
[SMILES]

439
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:29,017
Want me to take care of you?

440
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:30,268
What?

441
00:29:30,351 --> 00:29:31,644
[FLUSTERED]

442
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:35,648
I-HYEOK CUPS HYE-JU'S CHEEK

443
00:29:36,232 --> 00:29:37,442
Like this?

444
00:29:39,736 --> 00:29:43,072
HYE-JU LOOKS AT I-HYEOK NERVOUSLY

445
00:29:47,869 --> 00:29:50,371
I can do that romance thing for you.

446
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:53,625
So get more physical with me too.

447
00:29:57,962 --> 00:30:00,131
What a scumbag! Damn it!

448
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:01,800
What? Help me with the romance?

449
00:30:01,883 --> 00:30:04,385
So he'll date me in exchange
for some physical contact?

450
00:30:04,469 --> 00:30:05,804
Has he lost his mind?

451
00:30:06,304 --> 00:30:08,765
They said just being near him
was enough to charge him.

452
00:30:08,848 --> 00:30:10,892
Physical contact, my ass!

453
00:30:10,975 --> 00:30:12,101
Such a lowlife!

454
00:30:17,148 --> 00:30:18,483
That crazy jerk!

455
00:30:19,651 --> 00:30:21,820
She must still be in a lot of pain.

456
00:30:24,322 --> 00:30:26,616
Oh no. Our poor little sister.

457
00:30:36,876 --> 00:30:39,128
Are you sure you're okay to work already?

458
00:30:39,629 --> 00:30:42,090
I'm fine.
They wouldn't have let me out if I wasn't.

459
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:44,968
You didn't look fine at all earlier.

460
00:30:58,648 --> 00:31:00,275
Why is that lowlife…

461
00:31:07,907 --> 00:31:10,660
Get a table near that woman.

462
00:31:10,743 --> 00:31:12,453
Close to her. Over there.

463
00:31:12,954 --> 00:31:14,122
Wait. Why…

464
00:31:42,442 --> 00:31:43,276
All set, sir.

465
00:31:55,038 --> 00:31:56,873
What are you doing?

466
00:31:57,790 --> 00:31:59,751
I'm just being efficient.

467
00:32:00,627 --> 00:32:02,837
Should we start with this week's charges?

468
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:04,464
Two million?

469
00:32:05,256 --> 00:32:07,050
What do you mean, two million?

470
00:32:08,426 --> 00:32:09,302
No, thanks.

471
00:32:09,385 --> 00:32:11,429
-Don't bother the other--
-Thank you.

472
00:32:11,512 --> 00:32:14,682
This will be your table from now on, sir.

473
00:32:16,559 --> 00:32:18,269
Don't say a thing.

474
00:32:20,605 --> 00:32:21,439
What…

475
00:32:25,777 --> 00:32:26,653
Get to work.

476
00:32:34,869 --> 00:32:35,828
-Take care!
-Thanks.

477
00:32:35,912 --> 00:32:37,664
-See you next time!
-Thank you.

478
00:32:53,388 --> 00:32:55,098
We're closing, sir.

479
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:03,648
You don't have to clean this table.
I'll be back tomorrow.

480
00:33:05,191 --> 00:33:06,025
What?

481
00:33:06,901 --> 00:33:09,445
You plan to come here every day
for three months?

482
00:33:09,529 --> 00:33:10,363
This place is…

483
00:33:12,281 --> 00:33:15,159
This is an emergency charging station.

484
00:33:15,243 --> 00:33:17,578
"Emergency." Don't you know what it means?

485
00:33:19,831 --> 00:33:22,000
Every day is an emergency for me.

486
00:33:22,083 --> 00:33:23,876
And I still don't have your answer.

487
00:33:23,960 --> 00:33:26,254
About physical contact and romance.

488
00:33:27,797 --> 00:33:28,798
See

489
00:33:28,881 --> 00:33:29,757
you

490
00:33:30,258 --> 00:33:31,551
tomorrow.

491
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:16,846
Your drinks are ready.

492
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:51,839
Thank you.

493
00:35:39,387 --> 00:35:40,847
Don't come here anymore.

494
00:35:41,764 --> 00:35:45,393
You're the one who told me to come here.

495
00:35:46,644 --> 00:35:49,438
I specifically said not to come
unless you were dying.

496
00:35:49,522 --> 00:35:50,731
I told you, didn't I?

497
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:53,401
I feel like I'm dying
the moment you're not around.

498
00:35:56,529 --> 00:35:59,615
It's driving me crazy
only getting to see you like this.

499
00:36:00,283 --> 00:36:01,701
And now I can't come?

500
00:36:01,784 --> 00:36:03,077
Holy smokes.

501
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:05,621
Just stay with me.

502
00:36:06,747 --> 00:36:08,499
That's all you have to do.

503
00:36:11,878 --> 00:36:12,712
All right.

504
00:36:16,924 --> 00:36:18,009
-Come here.
-Why?

505
00:36:18,092 --> 00:36:19,385
Just come.

506
00:36:23,264 --> 00:36:24,182
What is it?

507
00:36:24,265 --> 00:36:27,727
Hey, why do you keep trying
to kick him out?

508
00:36:27,810 --> 00:36:30,021
He's bringing in more female customers.

509
00:36:30,104 --> 00:36:32,732
We were doing just fine without him.

510
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:35,693
Is "just fine" the same as "packed"? Huh?

511
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:42,283
And how did you meet
a guy that handsome and rich?

512
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:45,161
He's just a friend I met at the hospital.

513
00:36:45,244 --> 00:36:46,078
Does he like you?

514
00:36:46,162 --> 00:36:47,580
What about the electric shocks?

515
00:36:48,164 --> 00:36:49,957
He doesn't know about that, does he?

516
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:53,336
Goodness. I wish I could put you
in a full-body rubber suit.

517
00:36:53,419 --> 00:36:56,505
It's not like that. Stop talking nonsense.

518
00:36:59,508 --> 00:37:00,593
Get back here.

519
00:37:00,676 --> 00:37:01,552
What now?

520
00:37:01,636 --> 00:37:03,512
Don't go over there.

521
00:37:04,305 --> 00:37:05,306
Get back here.

522
00:37:49,892 --> 00:37:51,018
What the hell

523
00:37:52,478 --> 00:37:54,522
is draining the battery?

524
00:38:05,157 --> 00:38:07,451
How many days has it been
since I was discharged?

525
00:38:09,328 --> 00:38:10,329
Exactly one week, sir.

526
00:38:10,413 --> 00:38:14,041
I've only been doing
this frustrating, inefficient nonsense

527
00:38:15,626 --> 00:38:17,086
for a week?

528
00:38:17,169 --> 00:38:20,256
Three months will fly by.
Just hang in there a little longer.

529
00:38:20,339 --> 00:38:24,552
I played nice and gave her
the same smile I give everyone else.

530
00:38:26,220 --> 00:38:28,597
But she won't fall for it at all.

531
00:38:28,681 --> 00:38:31,183
You treated her like a lunatic
from the start.

532
00:38:31,267 --> 00:38:33,227
Of course she's not falling for it.

533
00:38:34,103 --> 00:38:35,021
When did I do that?

534
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:37,189
Well,

535
00:38:37,940 --> 00:38:39,608
even if you're dating,

536
00:38:39,692 --> 00:38:41,861
it's hard to be together all the time.

537
00:38:41,944 --> 00:38:43,362
Unless you live together.

538
00:38:44,322 --> 00:38:46,907
Live together?

539
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:54,248
Yes, Grandma.

540
00:38:55,374 --> 00:38:57,168
Yes, I'm on my way.

541
00:38:57,668 --> 00:38:58,669
All right.

542
00:38:59,670 --> 00:39:02,340
We'll stop by the resort,
then head to Pyeongchang-dong.

543
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:05,843
Are you sure
you don't need to see Ms. Na first?

544
00:39:08,471 --> 00:39:10,389
I'll wrap this up quick and head over.

545
00:39:32,703 --> 00:39:34,497
I thought you had plans in Sangam.

546
00:39:34,580 --> 00:39:36,165
Shouldn't you get going?

547
00:39:36,248 --> 00:39:37,833
Yeah. I should.

548
00:39:37,917 --> 00:39:39,126
A writers' meeting, right?

549
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:41,712
Yeah, with the girls
I went to the drama academy with.

550
00:39:41,796 --> 00:39:42,630
I'm off.

551
00:39:42,713 --> 00:39:43,589
Have fun.

552
00:39:43,672 --> 00:39:45,841
And one more thing…

553
00:39:49,220 --> 00:39:51,138
Never mind. Bye.

554
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:54,475
Bye.

555
00:40:18,707 --> 00:40:19,542
Ho-rang.

556
00:40:20,042 --> 00:40:22,169
What's with the face? Is something wrong?

557
00:40:22,837 --> 00:40:24,296
I've got a lot on my mind.

558
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:27,633
Are you really that incompetent
you have to bring work home?

559
00:40:28,717 --> 00:40:31,220
It wasn't for work.
I was just checking the time.

560
00:40:31,303 --> 00:40:33,013
Are you that eager to get home?

561
00:40:33,514 --> 00:40:37,226
Mom, you know Do-yoon
always manages his schedule well.

562
00:40:37,309 --> 00:40:40,563
He was in charge
of TS Hotel's 30th anniversary event,

563
00:40:41,439 --> 00:40:43,607
and he didn't look tired at all.

564
00:40:43,691 --> 00:40:45,317
He was flying around, Mom.

565
00:40:45,401 --> 00:40:47,069
-Literally flying.
-Me? I was?

566
00:40:47,153 --> 00:40:47,987
You little…

567
00:40:48,070 --> 00:40:51,198
Maybe he was too busy
making TS look bad to sleep.

568
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:55,035
Gosh, Mom. Those articles were written
to make him look bad.

569
00:40:55,119 --> 00:40:56,871
A cheek kiss in other countries?

570
00:40:56,954 --> 00:40:58,789
-It's just a greeting.
-Cut it out!

571
00:40:59,957 --> 00:41:02,251
We're lucky we could pay it off.

572
00:41:02,334 --> 00:41:05,337
Don't you know that's sexual harassment,
no matter the gender?

573
00:41:05,421 --> 00:41:06,255
That's hot.

574
00:41:06,338 --> 00:41:07,590
What the…

575
00:41:07,673 --> 00:41:10,176
How could you serve tea this hot?

576
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:11,093
Seriously!

577
00:41:11,635 --> 00:41:13,512
But Grandma,

578
00:41:14,013 --> 00:41:17,224
that only happened
because I got carried away at the club.

579
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:19,477
I was actually there for work.

580
00:41:19,560 --> 00:41:21,061
You know social media, right?

581
00:41:21,145 --> 00:41:23,397
Popular people on there
are called influencers--

582
00:41:23,481 --> 00:41:25,900
You think I don't know
what an influencer is?

583
00:41:26,484 --> 00:41:28,068
Our chairwoman never disappoints.

584
00:41:28,986 --> 00:41:30,196
Ho-rang.

585
00:41:31,030 --> 00:41:33,365
I heard you scored big
with the Jeju resort.

586
00:41:33,449 --> 00:41:36,368
Yes, it will help
with the rebranding as well.

587
00:41:37,036 --> 00:41:39,288
Now we just need to find our new face.

588
00:41:39,788 --> 00:41:42,833
I expect the brand value
to more than triple.

589
00:41:43,417 --> 00:41:46,962
If you'd just marry the heir to Hanlim,
it'd all fall into your lap.

590
00:41:47,046 --> 00:41:48,672
-How foolish.
-Mom!

591
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:51,759
Just set her up with Do-yoon.

592
00:41:51,842 --> 00:41:53,135
He doesn't even want her!

593
00:41:53,219 --> 00:41:56,180
Lower your voice.
You'll scare my Lucky Charm.

594
00:42:00,851 --> 00:42:02,645
You have a secret girlfriend?

595
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:10,736
You were in such a hurry to leave.

596
00:42:13,405 --> 00:42:15,950
I'm busy. I don't have time for you.

597
00:42:16,033 --> 00:42:18,035
You kept checking your watch at dinner.

598
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:19,954
Seeing someone?

599
00:42:20,746 --> 00:42:23,374
What's it to you what I look at?

600
00:42:23,457 --> 00:42:25,084
Get off my back, will you?

601
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:28,504
Just go humor Grandma for a bit
before you leave.

602
00:42:28,587 --> 00:42:31,006
That's what you're good at.
Acting all cute.

603
00:42:38,597 --> 00:42:40,432
Does Grandma know this side of him?

604
00:42:40,516 --> 00:42:42,893
That two-faced prick.

605
00:42:59,785 --> 00:43:00,911
Where's Ms. Na Bo-bae?

606
00:43:01,579 --> 00:43:02,538
Bo-bae had plans--

607
00:43:02,621 --> 00:43:03,747
Where is she?

608
00:43:04,915 --> 00:43:05,958
Why do you ask?

609
00:43:09,753 --> 00:43:11,255
I need to see her right now.

610
00:43:11,755 --> 00:43:13,424
Where is she?

611
00:43:15,676 --> 00:43:18,345
Ju-hee. Filming starts soon, right?

612
00:43:19,763 --> 00:43:20,598
Yeah.

613
00:43:21,390 --> 00:43:24,476
Kim Hae-ri is the female lead,
Kang Jun is the male lead,

614
00:43:24,560 --> 00:43:26,061
and Yeom Min-kyu is directing.

615
00:43:26,145 --> 00:43:29,189
It's already shaping up to be a big hit.

616
00:43:29,273 --> 00:43:33,902
Well, MBS is hyping it
as one of its most anticipated shows.

617
00:43:35,863 --> 00:43:36,989
What about you, Bo-bae?

618
00:43:37,781 --> 00:43:38,616
Huh?

619
00:43:39,783 --> 00:43:40,618
Me?

620
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:42,786
It's been ages. How have you been?

621
00:43:42,870 --> 00:43:45,122
Every time I see you,
you say you're writing.

622
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:47,166
Give us some updates.

623
00:43:49,293 --> 00:43:50,127
Oh.

624
00:43:51,128 --> 00:43:52,129
I'm…

625
00:43:55,424 --> 00:43:58,135
I'm also working with Director Yeom.

626
00:43:58,218 --> 00:44:01,138
We'll probably start production
after they finish shooting yours.

627
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:04,642
Director Yeom's next project is your work?

628
00:44:04,725 --> 00:44:07,394
That's amazing. Good for you.

629
00:44:07,478 --> 00:44:08,729
Congrats!

630
00:44:09,396 --> 00:44:12,900
The male lead has already been cast.
You know Ji Eun-ho, right?

631
00:44:12,983 --> 00:44:15,694
Ji Eun-ho?
I'm totally into him these days.

632
00:44:16,904 --> 00:44:18,822
Eun-ho and I are pretty close, you know.

633
00:44:18,906 --> 00:44:23,118
He's had dibs on the male lead
for the past three years.

634
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:27,039
So Eun-ho's confirmed as my male lead.

635
00:44:28,874 --> 00:44:31,126
He's a huge star now.
Does he even have time?

636
00:44:32,127 --> 00:44:34,546
Didn't he promise you that
before he made it?

637
00:44:34,630 --> 00:44:37,925
Really? I met him just a few days ago.

638
00:44:38,008 --> 00:44:39,968
We were still talking about the script.

639
00:44:40,052 --> 00:44:43,055
Though all I talked about
was how stressed I was over the script.

640
00:44:44,598 --> 00:44:45,891
But you know,

641
00:44:46,517 --> 00:44:49,019
you can't always trust what actors say.

642
00:44:49,895 --> 00:44:54,233
Top actors are usually booked
one or two years ahead.

643
00:44:54,316 --> 00:44:59,238
Why would Ji Eun-ho keep his schedule open
for a rookie writer's drama?

644
00:44:59,863 --> 00:45:01,782
Well, that's true.

645
00:45:01,865 --> 00:45:03,325
And technically, Bo-bae,

646
00:45:03,409 --> 00:45:06,620
you're not even a rookie yet.

647
00:45:06,704 --> 00:45:09,540
You're still just an aspiring writer.

648
00:45:15,462 --> 00:45:16,880
Hey, come on.

649
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:19,550
I'm the aspiring writer here.
Still entering contests.

650
00:45:19,633 --> 00:45:21,927
Bo-bae's already made her debut.

651
00:45:22,010 --> 00:45:24,096
Oh, right.

652
00:45:24,179 --> 00:45:26,056
She has made her debut.

653
00:45:30,352 --> 00:45:33,355
I was just worried about her. That's all.

654
00:45:34,523 --> 00:45:37,776
If Bo-bae takes an actor at his word
and the casting falls through,

655
00:45:37,860 --> 00:45:38,902
she's the one who pays.

656
00:45:39,486 --> 00:45:40,320
Bo-bae.

657
00:45:42,781 --> 00:45:43,615
Ji Eun-ho!

658
00:45:44,575 --> 00:45:46,076
Hey, Eun-ho.

659
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:48,787
I was passing by
after having dinner with the film crew.

660
00:45:49,663 --> 00:45:51,081
Are these your friends?

661
00:45:52,291 --> 00:45:53,876
Oh, hello.

662
00:45:55,043 --> 00:45:57,254
These are my drama academy classmates.

663
00:45:57,337 --> 00:45:59,548
-So you're all writers.
-Yes.

664
00:45:59,631 --> 00:46:03,093
We were actually just talking about you.

665
00:46:06,180 --> 00:46:07,014
Bo-bae.

666
00:46:07,973 --> 00:46:09,475
You only said nice things, right?

667
00:46:09,558 --> 00:46:10,976
Yeah. Of course.

668
00:46:12,186 --> 00:46:15,439
If you're heading out, I'll take you home.
I was passing by anyway.

669
00:46:16,023 --> 00:46:17,900
-Well…
-No, we're going to stay--

670
00:46:17,983 --> 00:46:20,611
Oh my. You two are really close!

671
00:46:20,694 --> 00:46:21,862
My gosh!

672
00:46:21,945 --> 00:46:23,822
-Go.
-Yeah, go now.

673
00:46:23,906 --> 00:46:24,907
-Go.
-Gosh.

674
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:27,785
Let's go.

675
00:46:29,244 --> 00:46:30,454
-Your bag.
-Yeah.

676
00:46:32,247 --> 00:46:34,124
All right. Get home safe.

677
00:46:34,625 --> 00:46:36,335
Bye!

678
00:46:42,090 --> 00:46:44,802
Seriously, how'd you pop up
out of nowhere?

679
00:46:44,885 --> 00:46:46,804
I thought I was seeing things.

680
00:46:46,887 --> 00:46:49,097
I came to the rescue
just in time, didn't I?

681
00:46:51,809 --> 00:46:53,685
Did you hear what I said?

682
00:46:55,187 --> 00:46:56,563
Just the last part?

683
00:46:57,940 --> 00:47:01,902
Writer Kang Ju-hee's the one
who kept picking on you, right?

684
00:47:03,111 --> 00:47:06,782
You told me about her,
but she's even worse in person.

685
00:47:06,865 --> 00:47:09,409
She's got "grumpy"
written all over her face.

686
00:47:10,828 --> 00:47:12,162
We all started together,

687
00:47:12,246 --> 00:47:14,706
but I'm the only one
still stuck in the same place.

688
00:47:14,790 --> 00:47:15,833
I must look pathetic.

689
00:47:16,750 --> 00:47:17,626
You? Why?

690
00:47:19,002 --> 00:47:21,046
No one writes as well as you.

691
00:47:22,256 --> 00:47:24,466
You know I became an actor because of you.

692
00:47:25,050 --> 00:47:25,884
"It's true."

693
00:47:25,968 --> 00:47:26,802
3 YEARS AGO

694
00:47:26,885 --> 00:47:29,221
"Trying for the civil service exam
at my age? Embarrassing."

695
00:47:29,930 --> 00:47:31,890
"But it's too urly to give up."

696
00:47:32,933 --> 00:47:34,977
"It's… it's too early. Too early."

697
00:47:35,060 --> 00:47:38,397
"But… but it's too early to give up."

698
00:47:38,480 --> 00:47:39,314
"It's too early."

699
00:47:41,859 --> 00:47:44,194
I'm sorry.

700
00:47:44,695 --> 00:47:45,988
Eun-ho.

701
00:47:46,655 --> 00:47:50,826
Don't tell me this is your first time
reading the script.

702
00:47:53,912 --> 00:47:54,997
I'm sorry.

703
00:47:55,080 --> 00:47:57,165
All right. Relax.

704
00:47:57,666 --> 00:48:00,961
For a one-episode drama,
we'll be here all night.

705
00:48:01,044 --> 00:48:03,046
I'm sorry.

706
00:48:03,130 --> 00:48:04,464
Okay. Let's try again.

707
00:48:10,345 --> 00:48:11,597
Ms. Writer.

708
00:48:15,475 --> 00:48:16,727
I'm sorry about earlier.

709
00:48:21,732 --> 00:48:23,442
Mr. Ji.

710
00:48:26,069 --> 00:48:27,779
You don't have to apologize.

711
00:48:28,363 --> 00:48:30,908
You just got too into the character.

712
00:48:31,617 --> 00:48:35,787
It actually helped me understand
who the character really was.

713
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:40,125
Even though I wrote it,
I was moved watching you act.

714
00:48:40,792 --> 00:48:43,295
Thank you for taking it so seriously.

715
00:48:43,378 --> 00:48:45,422
-I should be thanking you.
-I'm more grateful.

716
00:48:45,505 --> 00:48:46,506
-I am.
-No, I am.

717
00:48:46,590 --> 00:48:47,674
No, I'm really…

718
00:48:47,758 --> 00:48:49,509
Thank you. Really.

719
00:48:49,593 --> 00:48:52,095
I've been a fan of yours ever since.

720
00:48:53,931 --> 00:48:57,225
So don't let those words hurt you.

721
00:48:58,310 --> 00:48:59,811
Don't let them bring you down.

722
00:49:00,312 --> 00:49:01,396
Don't blame yourself.

723
00:49:03,982 --> 00:49:04,816
Okay.

724
00:49:12,532 --> 00:49:15,661
Bo-bae said she was meeting friends
in Sangam

725
00:49:15,744 --> 00:49:17,287
and would head home afterward.

726
00:49:35,222 --> 00:49:36,348
Bye.

727
00:49:36,431 --> 00:49:37,599
Thank you.

728
00:49:55,826 --> 00:49:59,371
THANK YOU FOR COMING TO US,
GREAT ACTOR JI EUN-HO

729
00:50:01,748 --> 00:50:03,542
I should thank you too.

730
00:50:03,625 --> 00:50:04,793
Thank you, but…

731
00:50:10,090 --> 00:50:13,010
VOICE OF THE NIGHT

732
00:50:14,219 --> 00:50:17,014
When I see things like this,
I can't help but wonder.

733
00:50:17,681 --> 00:50:19,850
Why does everyone else
seem to be moving forward

734
00:50:20,350 --> 00:50:22,477
while I'm still stuck in the same place?

735
00:50:30,444 --> 00:50:33,113
I don't have the talent or the means,

736
00:50:33,613 --> 00:50:35,866
but I'm way too proud to admit it.

737
00:50:35,949 --> 00:50:38,827
Pretending I've got it all together.
Pretending I've made it.

738
00:50:38,910 --> 00:50:41,288
Just pretending all the time.

739
00:50:42,622 --> 00:50:46,293
Why is everyone moving up except me?

740
00:50:48,295 --> 00:50:50,756
Take me with you.

741
00:52:01,451 --> 00:52:02,327
Get lost.

742
00:52:10,627 --> 00:52:13,171
Mr. Baek, how did you…

743
00:52:37,863 --> 00:52:39,197
Ms. Na.

744
00:52:39,906 --> 00:52:40,949
I had a plan.

745
00:52:41,992 --> 00:52:42,951
What?

746
00:52:43,034 --> 00:52:45,287
I was going to do all I could
to be around you

747
00:52:46,204 --> 00:52:47,455
and slowly

748
00:52:48,039 --> 00:52:50,083
win you over.

749
00:52:50,167 --> 00:52:51,001
What plan?

750
00:52:51,084 --> 00:52:52,961
Wait. Let go of me.

751
00:52:55,422 --> 00:52:56,631
But taking it slow…

752
00:52:59,301 --> 00:53:01,136
won't work anymore.

753
00:53:02,762 --> 00:53:04,181
I don't think I can do that.

754
00:53:05,515 --> 00:53:07,976
If anything happens to you…

755
00:53:10,103 --> 00:53:11,605
I'll die too.

756
00:53:20,447 --> 00:53:23,867
If you need anything for your script,
I'll help however I can.

757
00:53:25,285 --> 00:53:26,494
If you want,

758
00:53:26,578 --> 00:53:29,998
I'll say romantic things,
do romantic things, even act romantic.

759
00:53:30,707 --> 00:53:32,125
So move in with me.

760
00:53:32,709 --> 00:53:34,753
Stick to the physical contact
we agreed on.

761
00:53:34,836 --> 00:53:36,463
I'm not asking for much.

762
00:53:36,546 --> 00:53:38,089
Just holding hands is enough.

763
00:53:38,173 --> 00:53:41,468
Hey, wait. Just calm down.

764
00:53:42,052 --> 00:53:43,178
Did you just…

765
00:53:44,429 --> 00:53:46,723
Did you ask me to move in with you
and live together?

766
00:53:46,806 --> 00:53:47,641
Yes.

767
00:53:47,724 --> 00:53:50,518
I'm not going all over Seoul
looking for you again

768
00:53:50,602 --> 00:53:52,562
when I'm on the verge of dying.

769
00:53:52,646 --> 00:53:54,731
And I don't want you getting hurt or dying

770
00:53:54,814 --> 00:53:57,025
and leaving me unable to recharge.

771
00:53:57,525 --> 00:53:59,819
I need to keep you

772
00:54:00,320 --> 00:54:01,738
by my side.

773
00:54:04,074 --> 00:54:05,283
Right.

774
00:54:05,951 --> 00:54:09,246
So this was all about recharging?

775
00:54:19,005 --> 00:54:19,881
Could it be…

776
00:54:20,882 --> 00:54:21,841
Does…

777
00:54:21,925 --> 00:54:25,178
Does it get supercharged
when we're touching?

778
00:54:25,762 --> 00:54:27,305
"Supercharge"?

779
00:54:28,431 --> 00:54:30,475
I guess you could say that.

780
00:54:31,268 --> 00:54:33,812
The more intimate the contact,
the faster it charges.

781
00:54:35,397 --> 00:54:37,148
What? What in the world…

782
00:54:39,526 --> 00:54:41,278
Please save me, Ms. Na Bo-bae.

783
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:45,991
Just three months until the surgery.

784
00:54:47,784 --> 00:54:49,244
Recharge me.

785
00:54:53,331 --> 00:54:54,791
Three months.

786
00:54:54,874 --> 00:55:00,130
I'll give you three months
to come up with a sexy romance.

787
00:55:08,471 --> 00:55:09,389
Okay.

788
00:55:09,889 --> 00:55:11,141
I will…

789
00:55:13,393 --> 00:55:15,103
save you, Mr. Baek Ho-rang.

790
00:57:20,395 --> 00:57:25,108
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
